From a91a9592129d234cd9d2b414ef1130970220b1f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:38:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Network Manager in Settings > Apps > Network access

Port of the GrapheneOS-era Sable Network Manager (R9 settings
cohesion) to LineageOS. GrapheneOS made the Network permission
revocable; LineageOS does not, and instead already enforces a per-UID
network restriction that App info > Mobile data & Wi-Fi exposes
(NetworkPolicyManager.POLICY_REJECT_ALL and the per-transport bits).
Network Manager is one list over that same store
(DUPLICATE_NETWORK_POLICY_STORE=NO, no second blocker):

* one switch per app (per UID; shared-UID apps share a row), sorted by
  name, current user, apps the All apps list shows;
* the switch adds or removes only POLICY_REJECT_ALL; Wi-Fi, mobile
  data, VPN and background-data restrictions set in App info are shown
  in the row and kept;
* blocking an app that sends messages, mail or calls asks first;
* the page says what it does and does not do (no website/DNS filter).

Entry: Settings > Apps > Network access (searchable). Exported as
org.sableos.settings.NETWORK_MANAGER for Sable Tools, which sends the
action with no extras. Keyboard: type-ahead on app names, Home/End,
Page Up/Down, / or Ctrl+K for search (reusing the Battery keyboard
model); Space toggles through the platform switch.
